# A VS Code extension manifest must declare engines.vscode - vsce parses it to
# derive the minimum VS Code version and to check @types/vscode against it - but
# yarn 1 only recognises runtimes it knows (node, npm, yarn) and warns
# "The engine "vscode" appears to be invalid" on every single command.
#
# There is no way to exempt one key in yarn 1, so engine checking is off. The
# cost is that a dependency's node-version requirement would no longer be
# flagged; CI and development both pin Node 22, so nothing is relying on it.
--ignore-engines true
